   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Low VRAM (advanced)\n\nThe smallest published files: Base in HMS v1 (MOSS-Image_Base_HMS_v1, 3.96 GB) and the w4a8 text\nencoder (qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq, 7.3 GB), with Turbo 8-steps v1.0 (8 steps, CFG 1). 11.6 GB of files with\nthe VAE, against 20.3 GB for Base bf16 + the int8 text encoder.\n\nMeasured on an RTX 5090 (tools/RESULTS.md), a new prompt each image, against Base bf16 + int8 + the turbo:\n  whole card: 2.4 s an image (3.6 s), peak VRAM 10.8 GB (19.5 GB);\n  ComfyUI limited to about 8 GB (--reserve-vram 24, an emulation, not a smaller card): 2.7 s (4.5 s),\n  peak RAM of ComfyUI 5.2 GB (8.3 GB). First image 5.7 s (8.0 s).\nComfyUI moves weights between RAM and VRAM by itself, so the full files also ran in 8 GB here, 1.7x\n  slower; on your card and PCIe link the gap can differ.\nImages: 0.52 of a seed's difference from the full files (0.29 of it from the text encoder);\n  the harbor sign spelled right in 7 of 8 texts (the full files 8 of 8).\n\nModels: MOSS-Image_Base_HMS_v1 (huggingface.co/DeVilDoNia/MOSS-Image-HMS) in models/diffusion_models,\nqwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq (Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image) in models/text_encoders, the turbo LoRA in models/loras.\nAnother model to HMS v1: the HMS v1 Converter example (it needs the bf16 model in memory once)."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
